WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:03.420
Oppenheimer is one of the most&nbsp;
anticipated movies of the year.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:07.200
One of the many reasons for that could&nbsp;
be its strangely familiar leading man.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:12.060
There are quite a few familiar faces among the&nbsp;
cast for Christopher Nolan's new epic biographical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:17.400
drama Oppenheimer, including Marvel alum Robert&nbsp;
Downey Jr. and Midsommar star Florence Pugh.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:21.900
However, audiences may be most intrigued&nbsp;
by just how familiar the titular scientist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:25.440
J. Robert Oppenheimer himself, looks&nbsp;
to them — and it's not just because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:29.520
he's a well-known historical figure. As a&nbsp;
matter of fact, Oppenheimer is portrayed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:33.360
by one of Nolan's most long-standing&nbsp;
collaborators, actor Cillian Murphy.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:38.160
Murphy has been a notable name in film and TV&nbsp;
for decades at this point. In all of that time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:40.800
he's appeared in a number of&nbsp;
Nolan's most popular movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:44.760
but he has also featured in plenty of&nbsp;
notable productions outside of that sphere.

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:49.620
Murphy began work as an actor in 1996,&nbsp;
mainly appearing in theatrical productions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:53.520
small movies, and short films. The&nbsp;
now-renowned actor's breakout role was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:57.660
actually as the lead of Danny Boyle's&nbsp;
2002 apocalypse movie 28 Days Later.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:01.020
In the film, Murphy portrays&nbsp;
a bicycle courier named Jim,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:05.880
who awakens from a coma to find that society&nbsp;
has collapsed due to a virus that makes hosts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:10.680
incredibly aggressive. Together with several&nbsp;
other non-infected people, Jim fights to survive.

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:15.660
In a 2022 interview with NME looking&nbsp;
back on 28 Days Later, Murphy credited&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:19.260
the film as having helped him establish&nbsp;
him in the film industry. In retrospect,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:23.760
it could even be viewed as the first domino that&nbsp;
led to his role as Oppenheimer. He explained,

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:27.060
"It opened doors for me. I managed&nbsp;
to get meetings. I met Christopher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:29.040
Nolan through that, so it was massive for me."

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:33.120
Not long after 28 Days Later, Murphy&nbsp;
entered the world of superhero stardom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:37.320
in his first project with Nolan:&nbsp;
2005's Batman Begins. The first film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:41.700
in Nolan's Dark Knight trilogy starred Murphy&nbsp;
opposite Christian Bale as the DC vigilante.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:46.500
In the movie, Murphy plays Batman's nemesis,&nbsp;
Scarecrow, a sadistic psychologist who uses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:51.360
a specialized fear toxin to drive his victims&nbsp;
mad. Murphy's Scarecrow would only be a main&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:55.380
antagonist for the first movie in the trilogy,&nbsp;
but he nevertheless returned as the character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.380 --> 00:02:01.200
in cameo roles for the subsequent entries, 2008's&nbsp;
The Dark Knight and 2012's The Dark Knight Rises.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:05.280
A popular bit of trivia for Batman Begins&nbsp;
is that Murphy initially auditioned for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:09.240
the role of Batman. Of course, he didn't&nbsp;
land the part, but he did impress Nolan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:12.660
enough to get a major part and become&nbsp;
one of his most trusted collaborators.

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:15.900
While Nolan's Dark Knight trilogy&nbsp;
was still playing out in 2010,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:19.440
Murphy joined the esteemed director&nbsp;
for Inception, the twist-filled,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:23.160
mind-bending epic now considered to be&nbsp;
one of the best action movies of all time.

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:28.380
In the movie, Leonardo DiCaprio's Dom Cobb&nbsp;
leads a team in performing a dream-based heist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:32.760
in order to topple a business empire. Murphy&nbsp;
plays Robert Fischer, their unassuming target&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:36.420
who gets wrapped up in life-threatening&nbsp;
thrills when the heist goes sideways.

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:42.300
"I said right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:42.825
now! Right now."

00:02:42.825 --> 00:02:42.840
"5 2 8 4 9 1."

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:46.020
In an interview with Collider around&nbsp;
the time that Inception released,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:50.640
Murphy spoke at length about why he enjoys&nbsp;
working with Nolan as a filmmaker. He explained,

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:54.420
"For him the performance is paramount.&nbsp;
It's the connection between the actors.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:58.860
He allows room for spontaneity. You know&nbsp;
you would imagine spontaneity in a $200&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:03.060
million movie is not particularly high on&nbsp;
the list of priorities but for Chris it is."

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:06.660
Not content to simply become a dominant&nbsp;
force in the world of modern movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:11.280
Murphy also starred as the lead of one of&nbsp;
the most popular TV shows of the 2010s:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:13.920
the gritty period crime drama Peaky Blinders.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:18.420
In the series, Murphy portrays early 20th&nbsp;
century gang leader Tommy Shelby throughout&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:23.340
all six seasons. As Shelby, Murphy goes to&nbsp;
very dark and vulnerable places over the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:27.240
course of the series, and his performance&nbsp;
has been recognized with several awards.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:32.340
"Open your eyes, or I will cut&nbsp;
away your f------ eyelids."

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:35.580
In the beginning of his nearly&nbsp;
10-year period filming Peaky Blinders,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:39.300
Murphy had reservations about the&nbsp;
role. However, the long-term nature&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:42.960
of the project ultimately turned out to be&nbsp;
a uniquely fulfilling experience for him.

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:46.620
Speaking about how playing Tommy was&nbsp;
different from any other role he's had,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:48.360
Murphy told Entertainment Weekly,

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:51.780
"I did lots of other things, but I've&nbsp;
never had that experience of growing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:54.180
older with a character or being able to inhabit it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:57.000
to a point where the character starts&nbsp;
thinking for you in the performance."

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:00.900
One of Murphy's more recent cinematic&nbsp;
roles of note saw the actor once again&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:03.960
diving into full-fledged horror.&nbsp;
While he wasn't in the original,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:08.880
Murphy joined the cast of John Krasinski's&nbsp;
popular scare flick A Quiet Place Part II.

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:11.700
Murphy plays Emmett, an old&nbsp;
family friend of the Abbotts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:15.360
who helps Evelyn and her kids fight back&nbsp;
against the bloodthirsty aliens that have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:18.840
conquered Earth. Murphy amps up the&nbsp;
emotion in his portrayal of Emmett,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:22.980
who starts off in a morose state due to the death&nbsp;
of his family. Over the course of the movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:27.540
Emmett forges a trusted bond with young Regan,&nbsp;
and regains his sense of humanity and hope.

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:29.580
In an interview with The Hollywood Reporter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:33.780
Murphy noted that his mostly non-verbal&nbsp;
role in A Quiet Place Part II was unique,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:38.460
in that it allowed him to reach back to some of&nbsp;
his earliest experiences acting. He explained,

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:42.840
"I did theater for about four or five years&nbsp;
before I ever did any screen work. So I feel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:46.020
like I've done a lot of physical acting,&nbsp;
and since I've continued to do theater,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:50.220
it was a real sort of liberating experience&nbsp;
to get to explore some of that on screen."

